  <main_text>
    <l n="1">cundum juris Præceptum;</l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>alterum non lædes.</i> Quod enim</l>
    <l n="3">in thesi ita obtiner, id in hypo-</l>
    <l n="4">thesi aliter sese habet; &amp; ali-</l>
    <l n="5">quid indefinite illicitum judi-</l>
    <l n="6">catur quod tamen in circum-</l>
    <l n="7">stantiis censebitur esse licitum.</l>
    <l n="8">Non itaque alterum lædes nisi</l>
    <l n="9">cum te aliter tueri non potes,</l>
    <l n="10">neque occides, nisi licite, id est,</l>
    <l n="11">adhibito moderamine incul-</l>
    <l n="12">patæ tutelæ. Neque 3. obstat</l>
    <l n="13">dictum Valentiniani, Impera-</l>
    <l n="14">toris, <i>Homicida, quod fecit exspe-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>ctet.</i> Respondeo enim dictum</l>
    <l n="16">illud accipi oportere, de homi-</l>
    <l n="17">cidâ dolosò quique extra cau-</l>
    <l n="18">sam justæ defensionis huma-</l>
    <l n="19">num sanguinem effundit. Ut</l>
    <l n="20">secus dicendum sit, si quisquam</l>
    <l n="21">urgente necessitate adversario</l>
    <l n="22">necem intentaverit.</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">Concordant etiam juri ci-</l>
    <l n="24">vili canones, qui licitam sta-</l>
    <l n="25">tuunt sui defensionem, modo</l>
    <l n="26">ea cum moderamine sit con- jun-</l>
  </main_text>
